From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Daniel <egdaniel@google.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:02:27 -0400
Subject: [M156] [Ganesh] Do not drop subset clamp for nearest filtering on
 touching edges

Original change's description:
> [Ganesh] Do not drop subset clamp for nearest filtering on touching edges
>
> safe_to_ignore_subset_rect() assumed that with nearest filtering and no
> AA "the sampler shouldn't overshoot" a local quad whose edge coincides
> with the subset edge. On real hardware, texture units convert scaled
> coordinates to fixed-point with round-to-nearest (e.g. D3D11 >= 8
> fractional bits, Vulkan subTexelPrecisionBits >= 4), snapping coordinates
> close to the boundary onto the texel just outside the subset when
> magnified above 2^precision.
>
> This change:
> 1. Replaces the touching-edges bypass in safe_to_ignore_subset_rect()
>    with a check for 1:1 scale and integer relative translation
>    (including 90/180/270 degree rotations and flips). Under 1:1 integer
>    translations, sample centers land on exact half-integers in texel
>    space (at least 0.5 texels from any subset edge), making nearest
>    sampling safe from overshoot without shader clamping.
> 2. Lifts the safe_to_ignore_subset_rect() check into TextureOp::Make()
>    so non-kSrcOver draws (which fall back to FillRectOp) also drop
>    subset clamping on 1:1 integer draws.
> 3. Fixes the nearest-filter domain safety check in GrTextureEffect::
>    Sampling() to verify that r.fShaderClamp contains domain, preventing
>    incorrect removal of shader clamping for fractional domains near
>    the subset boundary.
> 4. Updates Device_drawTexture to buffer safeBounds by kLinearInset for
>    all filters on approx-fit proxies, ensuring kFast is upgraded to
>    kStrict when the src rect reaches the proxy boundary.
> 5. Adds TextureOpNearestSubsetOvershootTest to verify nearest-neighbor
>    sampling against subset edges across magnification, 1:1 integer
>    and fractional translations, rotations, flips, and approx proxies.
>
